5.270.m:
The tortoise said:
There is a brahmin seer named Mārkaṇḍa, who indeed remembers seven aeons;
and he was brought, O virtuous sage, by this king Indradyumna,

Bhartṛyajña said:
Lomaśa then spoke to him: “Ask with confidence, O king;
I shall certainly tell you whatever you ask me.”

Indradyumna said:
You are heard of by all creatures as being long-lived;
therefore I too have arrived with a desire for your darśana.

Lomaśa said:
Whenever an aeon arrives, one hair of mine falls out;
and upon the disappearance of all hairs, then my destruction will occur.

My father, out of great affection, applied remedies,
and spells for the sake of speech, as well as vows and offerings;
he constantly questioned brahmins, unwearied by day and night.

Bhartṛyajña said:
“A golden Meru should be given; Kailāsa made of silver;
Himādri out of cotton; and Gandhamādana made of jaggery;

5.275.m:
“Going ahead of everyone, [we will see] Hāṭakeśvara in Pātāla;
